{"id": "P08379", "name": "Roger Federer", "name_chinese": "罗杰·费德勒", "country": "Switzerland", "net_worth_usd_m": "948.9", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time (former)", "source_of_wealth": "Tennis", "industry": "sports", "sec_insider_companies": "", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (former) (2026); Hurun Global (2023-2026)", "focus": [], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/roger-federer/", "wikidata_url": "", "forbes_bio": ["During a pro tennis career in which he won 20 Grand Slam singles titles, Roger Federer had a sponsor portfolio that was unmatched in the sports world. At his peak, he earned $100 million off the court in a single year.", "Federer also won more than $130 million in ATP Tour prize money before retiring in 2022. Only Novak Djokovic and Rafael Nadal have exceeded that total.", "Many brands, including Mercedes and Rolex, have stuck with Federer since he hung up his racket. His biggest deal is with Uniqlo apparel, which signed him in 2018 for ten years and $300 million.", "His biggest win has been an estimated 3% stake in Swiss athletic apparel company On, which went public in 2021.", "Federer's namesake foundation supports education in Southern Africa and Switzerland. It says it has spent nearly $100 million and benefited more than 3 million children since its launch in 2003."], "forbes_facts": ["Federer was the world's highest-paid athlete in 2020, taking in an estimated $106.3 million before taxes and agents' fees.", "Born to a notable Swiss family, Federer started playing tennis at age 3 while accompanying his parents to their employer's private courts on weekends."]}
